  "title": "Erdős Problem #995",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $n_1<n_2<\\cdots$ be a lacunary sequence of integers and $f\\in L^2([0,1])$. Estimate the growth of, for almost all $\\alpha$, $ \\sum_{1\\leq k\\leq N}f(\\{ \\alpha n_k\\}). $ For example, is it true that, for almost all $\\alpha$, $ \\sum_{1\\leq k\\leq N}f(\\{ \\alpha n_k\\})=o(N\\sqrt{\\log\\log N})? $ ",
